# PitchPerfect MVP

## Stack
Next.js 14+ App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS 3.4+, shadcn/ui,
Zustand 4.x, OpenAI Realtime API, Claude Sonnet for feedback, Vercel KV, PostHog, Vercel hosting.

## Architecture
- 3 screens: /setup -> /session -> /feedback. Linear flow. No branching.
- NO user accounts, NO login, NO auth, NO database. Vercel KV only.
- ConversationProvider interface in src/lib/conversation/types.ts abstracts AI provider.
- Frontend NEVER talks to OpenAI directly. Always via /api/realtime WebSocket relay.
- All KV operations through src/lib/storage.ts. Never import @vercel/kv elsewhere.
- Session state machine in Zustand: idle->configuring->ready->connecting->active->ending->feedback

## Code Standards
- Functional components only. function keyword, not arrows, for component declarations.
- Props use interfaces. Named exports only (except page.tsx).
- No enums. Use const objects with 'as const'.
- No inline styles. Tailwind only. cn() for conditional classes from src/lib/utils.ts.
- Event handlers: handleClick, handleSubmit, etc.
- Import order: react/next -> third-party -> @/lib -> @/components -> @/stores -> @/types -> relative
- Colors: primary indigo-600, success emerald-600, warning amber-600, error red-600.
- Desktop-first. No dark mode. No mobile optimization for MVP.

## Forbidden
- Never create: Docker files, CI/CD configs, database migrations, auth configs.
- Never use: Redux, MobX, Context for state, CSS modules, styled-components, Socket.io.
- Never install: prisma, drizzle, next-auth, clerk, socket.io, express.
- Never use 'any' type. Use 'unknown' for truly unknown values.

## After EVERY change
- Run: npm run type-check (tsc --noEmit)
- Run: npm run lint
- Verify no new TypeScript errors introduced.
- Don't do anything else beyond the specific task requested.
